== GR-13: who reads a 0057DAD0 row's price, and does such a list reach the driver
PASS  A1a cursors: 0057DAD0 rbx = entry + 8, r14 = rbx - 8 = entry; 0057DED0 rbx / 0057DD60 rdi = entry + 0x10
PASS  A1b entry offsets written (structflow, stride 0x20): 0057DAD0 +00 +08 +0A +0C +0E +10; 0057DD60 +00 +08 +0A +0C +0E +10; 0057DC30 +00 +08 +0A +0C +0E +10; 0057DED0 +00 +08 +0A +0B +0C +0E +10
PASS  A1c 0057DAD0's price dword and zero-price bit land at entry +0x10 (0057DB9F, 0057DBCC, 0057DBE0; bts at 0057DBDC); its id at +8 (0057DB7E), its name pointer at +0 (0057DB98)
PASS  A2a 0057CF20 hands its list to all four fillers at 11 sites (0057D197, 0057D20E, 0057D25C, 0057D2D9, 0057D322, 0057D352, 0057D3D9, 0057D411, 0057D48D, 0057D4B6, 0057D4D2) and returns it (ret 0057D513)
PASS  A2b the returned list escapes only at 005655F0 005656AE and 00565720 00565785 (mov [rdi + 0xe0], rax); no copy, no indirect call
PASS  A2c 0057D620 calls the fillers at 9 sites, each with rcx = 0 (xor ecx, ecx) - it counts, it builds no list; 0057D610 is its only caller (a jmp)
PASS  A3a holder-field census at its fixpoint: shop/driver closure 37 sites (depth 3 = depth 12), list-widget closure 39 +0xE0 sites (depth 5 = depth 12); closure limited to 00560000-0057FFFF and 003FC000-003FFFFF
PASS  A3b 41 typed seed loads, all inside the census; the 30 other census sites are null tests, stores or the shop widget's child pointer (0056C815, 0056DDEC, 0056DE13, 0056E0D0)
PASS  A4a every dword read of a row's +0x10 outside the fillers (14): 0056CC7E, 0056CCA2, 0056CE07, 0056CE31, 0056CFF3, 0056D023, 0056D0C8, 0056D267, 0056D291, 0056D461, 0056D8F1, 0056DBCA, 0056E71A, 0056E797
PASS  A4b each of them either compares the whole dword with 0x80000000 (5 sites: 0056CC7E, 0056CE07, 0056CFF3, 0056D267, 0056E71A) or clears bit 31 of the loaded value within the next eight instructions before any other use (9 sites)
PASS  A4c every +0x08 read outside the fillers is a word, the id (34 sites, the driver's 0056D464 among them); none reads a price there
PASS  A4d the only non-filler writers of +0x10..+0x15 are 005651E0 (message 26, 16 stores), 00564650 (the reset, 0056468E / 00564692) and 00565BD0 (whole-row moves, 00565C7B / 00565C92) - all list-widget (family A) bodies
PASS  A4e with the holders seeded the list escapes at the same two widget stores, the driver's +0xC8 (0056E55A), its row pointer +0xD0 (0056D56F) and one family-A row pointer handed to a constructor message (005665B0 00566631, not followed); the driver's row reaches 0056E700 from 0056C7AF, 0056CB2C, 0056D576 and 0056D9F7
PASS  A5 sale mode (driver +0xD8 bit 0, the commit's 0056D46F bit): a row whose +0x10 dword is >= 0x80000000 scores 8 in 0056E700 and the driver declines it (0056D57B); the sell tab id 0x5A2 sets the sale bit (0056DE3D-0056DE72 -> 0056C950 -> 0056D71D)
PASS  A6 selectors routed to 0057DAD0: 0x04, 0x06, 0x07, 0x0C, 0x0F, 0x18, 0x1B; the zero-price flag 0x20 only for 0x0F (0057D3EA-0057D3F0)
PASS  A7 002FABD0 nibble table 00D0F990 = [4, -1, 7, 6, 5, 8, 9, 10]: id nibble 2 (0x2xxx) -> category 7; shop category = selector - 0x14 (0057CFB9), so 0x1B is category 7 = loot; category->class 00D113B8[7] = 7 = 0057DAD0's class on tail arm 3
== GR-14: can message 26's layout write land on a shop list
PASS  B1 005651E0 is entered only by tail jumps from 005636F0@00563721, 00563930@00563953, 00563B10@00563B41, 00563D20@00563D43; no rip reference, no data qword
PASS  B2 the four procedures are named only by leas in 00564B90 (00564C0A, 00564C13, 00564C1C, 00564C25) and by no data qword; 00564AC0 -> 00244F50 -> 002465F0 stores the procedure at widget +0 (00246641)
PASS  B3 00564B90 creates a list-procedure widget only for ids 0x405..0x40F (jump table 00564C4C): 405->kind 0/005636F0, 406->kind 1/005636F0, 407->kind 2/005636F0, 408->kind 3/005636F0, 409->kind 4/00563930, 40D->kind 5/00563B10, 40E->kind 6/00563930, 40F->kind 7/00563D20; 0x40A-0x40C get no procedure and 00564AC0 then creates nothing (00564B1D)
PASS  B4 the shop widget's procedure 0056E140 (installed only at 0056DD66) handles messages [1, 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, 15, 18, 19, 20] and sends 26 to 005C5230 (xor eax, eax / ret); the driver 0056D370 (installed only at 0056C9BC) sends it there too (0056D3B8)
PASS  B5 in the shop/driver closure +0xE0 is stored only at 0056563E, 005656AE, 0056E398, 0056E561; 005655F0's callers are the list families' creators (003FD6B0, 003FD860, 003FDAD0, 00564010, 00564E10) and 0056E410, which moves the list at 0056E55A
PASS  B6 message 26 is sent by the list-control draw bodies 002D2600 / 002D28E0 (only from 002D1420) through the target's own procedure (call rax = qword [target]); the shop list control forwards it to the driver, which routes it to the stub
